 "answer_text": "Found 4 disease records for brca1: Familial cancer of breast [3], Familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1 [4], Pancreatic cancer susceptibility 4 [5] and Fanconi anemia complementation group S [6]. \n\nThe gene, designated BRCA1, encodes a nuclear phosphoprotein that maintains genomic stability and acts as a tumor suppressor [1] [2]. Mutations in BRCA1 are responsible for approximately 40% of inherited breast cancers and more than 80% of inherited breast and ovarian cancers [2]. \n\nDisease records found\n\nDisease name: Familial cancer of breast [3]. Disease name: Familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1 [4]. Disease name: Pancreatic cancer susceptibility 4 [5]. Disease name: Fanconi anemia complementation group S [6]. \n\nGene records found\n\nGene symbol: BRCA1 [1]. Gene name: BRCA1 [10]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Mechanisms of Therapy Resistance in Patient-Derived Xenograft Models of BRCA1-Deficient Breast Cancer [7]. Pubmed title: BRCA1: An Endocrine and Metabolic Regulator [12]. Pubmed title: Preneoplastic stromal cells promote BRCA1-mediated breast tumorigenesis [15]. Pubmed title: Mechanism of BRCA1-BARD1 function in DNA end resection and DNA protection [18]. Pubmed title: Targeting GPX4-mediated ferroptosis protection sensitizes BRCA1-deficient cancer cells to PARP inhibitors [21]. \n\nClinvar records found\n\nClinvar title: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.5243_5277+2788del [8]. Clinvar title: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.5277+2916_5277+2946delinsGG [13]. Clinvar title: NG_005905.2:g.(147057_150288)_(160933_166866)del [16]. Clinvar title: GRCh37/hg19 17q21.31(chr17:41267743-41267796)x3 [19]. Clinvar title: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.2145C>G (p.Thr715=) [22]. \n\nOmim records found\n\nBRCA1 DNA REPAIR-ASSOCIATED PROTEIN [9]. BRCA1 [9]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: Germline BRCA1 and BRCA2 Mutations in Jewish Women Affected by Breast Cancer [11]. Clinical trial name: BRCA1 Haploinsufficiency and Gene Expression [14]. Clinical trial name: Study to Evaluate Treatment Customized According to RAP80 and BRCA1 in Patients With Advanced Lung Carcinoma [17]. Clinical trial name: Letrozole in Preventing Breast Cancer in Postmenopausal Women With a BRCA1 or BRCA2 Mutation [20]. Clinical trial name: Recombinant Human Chorionic Gonadotropin in Preventing Breast Cancer in Premenopausal Women With BRCA1 Mutations [23]. "
